  "excerpt": "Blanquette is a French white stew where the meat is never browned. Instead it is poached gently in stock with vegetables and finished with a rich, velvety sauce made from the cooking liquor, cream, and egg yolks. This version uses pork loin in place of veal. Quietly impressive.",
